{
  "_README": [
    "Question provenance — who wrote each live question, and in which batch.",
    "The join the scorecard's `production` section (D97) reads to measure",
    "farm vintages against editorial questions from the same k-floored",
    "aggregates it already fetches. Keys are bank ids per surface; rows are",
    "{ archiveId (daily only — the dq/dqx id the entry was promoted from),",
    "source: editorial|farm|community, batch: a vintage label — a date for",
    "generated batches, 'prototype' for the v9 port }.",
    "",
    "Maintained by machines where possible: promote-questions.mjs writes the",
    "daily rows (--source is required since D97; --batch labels the vintage,",
    "defaulting to the promotion date); feed rows ride the feed lane's PRs.",
    "check:quality holds this file exactly in",
    "step with the banks, both directions — a missing row is a CI failure,",
    "not a silent drop from the vintage rollup.",
    "",
    "Backfill provenance (2026-08-11): block boundaries read from the",
    "archive's own dated comments in src/v2/spec/daily-questions.js —",
    "indexes 0-52 editorial (prototype port + deeper archive), 53-64 farm",
    "2026-07-30 (PR #32), 65-89 editorial authoring session 2026-08-01",
    "(D30). All 73 feed questions are the prototype extraction (D52).",
    "`review` (farm/community rows only): who read this question before it entered the bank. { by: 'ai'|'human', at: date, audited?: bool } — D162. `by: 'human'` is the pre-D162 process, where a person read every candidate, and stays valid for anything a person still reads. `by: 'ai'` requires an explicit `audited` boolean: whether this row was in the human sample. Editorial rows carry no review because editorial IS the human."
  ],
